==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Dober]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Shachiko]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**1 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Like in [[Bamboocopter Launch]] and [[Broadleaf Yo-Yo]], the best way to deal with Shachiko is to nuke it with [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] after hitting the enemy base. Once that's done, you're left with a cleanup between Dark Dober and Gokurakko. This seems a bit challenging, but it's nothing that units like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] and [[Can Can Cat]] shouldn't be able to take care of.

==Trivia==
*Like most [[Forest Playground]] stages, Waterweed Trumpet's Japanese name is a reference to a toy. In this case, Piropiro Fue Mizukusa (ピロピロ笛水草, "Party Horn Waterweed") refers to [[wikipedia:Party horn|party horns]].

